      "content": "It is completely understandable to feel that surface-level fixes won't touch the depth of what you are feeling right now. When a core vision fades, it can feel like the foundation of your entire self has crumbled. Right now, instead of focusing on rebuilding the old vision, could you consider focusing on what is *different* about you now? Sometimes, a new sense of purpose emerges from acknowledging the end of an old one.",
      "source": "target",
